Z||000000||spideyfoot||05-18-2001||07:04 PM||||Im going to look at a 99,000 mile Formula . Black good paint new cluth motor externals gone over. Typical rip inn driver seat. Asking $2,900 how low do you think I<BR>should offer him. What are some possible problems I should look for. How should I check it for overheating. Thanks Folks <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||05-18-2001||08:05 PM||||Definately talk him down some.  I bought my Formula in 96 with 67K miles!  That isn't a bad price IMO, but he should move some.  Things to look at... shocks/struts, ball joints, brakes, tie rods... basically all the suspension stuff.  This stuff is expensive on the 88's and if it needs new brakes, rotors and calipers it will cost a decent $ for parts.<P>Also see how it idles when you first start it (cold) and after it warms up.  A high idle could mean it needs a new EGR tube or there is a cracket vacumn line.  Both seem to be common problems, and the EGR tube is apx. $100.  Other than that, make sure it runs good and seems to have good pick up.<P>It sounds good so far!  Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||05-18-2001||09:16 PM||||Spidey, Ive got a Formula (red) that Im wanting to sell....cheaper, and Im not too far from your town either. Email if interested.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||05-18-2001||09:32 PM||||What formula88 said. Th price is a little high for the mileage. My car had 48k on it when I bought it in 99 and it needed brakes, front ball joints, and rear wheel bearings because the owner drove the car with the emergency brakes on.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||spideyfoot||05-18-2001||10:55 PM||||Youve got mail my7||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||05-19-2001||11:19 AM||||Well, let's see, last January, I got my Formula, 98000 miles, needing brakes and a clutch for $2400.  But the paint is in great shape, the mechanicals are great, and the interior is damn near mint - so I'm not complaining.  Blue book on it (after brakes and clutch) is about $3800, so that's a good guide.  I'd probably offer about $2500 and go from there.  Even at $2900, you could do better, but you're not getting ripped off.  Good Luck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
